Third-party code
----------------

ExtPay.js (https://github.com/Glench/ExtPay) is licensed under the AGPLv3,
not the MIT License. It is used only for the optional Pro purchase flow.

It is deliberately NOT bundled into TabNap's own code. The build copies
it verbatim to extpay/ExtPay.js as a separate, unmodified file, so the two
licences stay clearly separable. The service worker loads it with
importScripts() at startup (MV3 only permits that at startup), but nothing runs and no
request is made until a user actively starts a purchase. It is omitted from the
build entirely while payment is unconfigured.
